  "description": "OQACES crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H65 Dy4 N8 O16,C55 H60 Dy4 N7 O16 2+,2.75(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(N1 O3 1-),4(C2 H6 O1),0.2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy12 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy22 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy32 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy42 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy21 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy31 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy41 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.515-4.098 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.61-117.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(HL^H)(L^H)2(OH)2(HCOO)(H2O)2(DMF)][Dy4(HL^H)(L^H)2(OH)2(HCOO)(H2O)(DMF)2](NO3)2·(H2O)0.2·(DMF)2.75. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 0 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
